<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
  <head>
    <link rel='stylesheet' href='/stylesheets/style.css'>
    <link rel='stylesheet' href='/stylesheets/media.css'>
    <link rel='stylesheet' href='/bootstrap/dist/css/bootstrap.min.css'>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/fontawesome-free-7.3.1-web/css/all.css">
    <script src="/bootstrap/dist/js/bootstrap.bundle.min.js"></script>

    <link href='https://fonts.googleapis.com/css?family=Inter' rel='stylesheet'>
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  </head>
    <body>
    <%- include("../partials/main_nav.ejs") %>     
      <div class="container-fluid mx-auto w-75">
        <section>
          <article>
            <h1 class="mt-5"><%= title %></h1>
            <p>A small guide on kanban boards and this project.</p>
            <hr> <!-- This is used as a horizontal separator between content. -->

            <p>
              This web application is designed so that you can create your own Kanban board! <br><br>
              
              Kanban boards are a project management tool designed and derived from the <a href="https://www.pmi.org/disciplined-agile/agile/whatisagile">Agile framework</a>. 
              Invented by Taiichi Ohno, a Japanese Industral Engineer at Toyota in the late 1940s, it was intended to visualize all of your 
              individual work tasks and the specific stages of progress that they are in. 
              
              <figure>
                <figcaption class="blockquote-footer mt-3">
                  Think of it like a board with sticky notes all around, categorizing their progress in columns.
                </figcaption>
              </figure>

          </article>

          <article>
            <h1 class="mt-3">How to Use</h1>
            <p>A guide on how to create, edit and view your board.</p>
            <hr> <!-- This is used as a horizontal separator between content. -->

            <p>
              First and foremost, you will need an account! You just need to head to the <a href="/boards">Boards</a>, 
              <a href="/register">Register</a>, or <a href="/login">Login</a> page. 

              Once you've created an account and have logged in you will be redirected to the Boards page, where you will
              see a "Create Your Board!" button. Click it and fill out the required fields.

              <figure>
                <figcaption class="blockquote-footer mt-3">
                  You will be prompted to enter a column and board name. This is to create your column and initialize your board.
                </figcaption>
              </figure>
              Congratulations! You've made your first column for your kanban board. You'll be greeted by a few extra buttons, as you
              navigate through your created board. These buttons and their functions are listed below.
            </p>

            <img src="/images/kb_example_updated.png" class="rounded image-fluid mt-3 mb-3 w-100">

          </article> 

        </section>
      </div>

    <%- include("../partials/footer.ejs") %>
    </body>
    
</html>